- Windows Task Manager now shows fleetd as "Fleet" instead of "Orbit osquery runtime and autoupdater". App Control for Business (WDAC) rules that match orbit.exe by file description need the new name; the product name stays "Fleet osquery".
- **Breaking change:** Once the Fleet server is on Fleet 5, fleetd renames its Windows Installed apps entry from "Fleet osquery" to "Fleet", and its Linux process from `orbit` to `Fleet`. Service names, the launchd label, the systemd unit, package names, install paths and the installer name don't change. Update policies, scripts and monitoring that look for the name "Fleet osquery" on Windows or the process name `orbit` on Linux.
